# Old ticket, booking and merch URLs that people may still have saved. Sending
# them to the closing page explains what happened instead of showing a 404.
#
# 302 rather than 301: a permanent redirect is cached by the browser
# indefinitely and would be painful to undo if any of these paths came back.
#
# NOTE: no "/*" catch-all here. Unlike Express -- where the static handler ran
# first and the catch-all only ever saw true misses -- Cloudflare Pages
# evaluates _redirects BEFORE serving static assets, so "/*" matches "/" and
# every asset too and the site redirects to itself forever. Only specific
# legacy paths are listed, and the 404 page below catches anything else.

/reserve            /  302
/reserve/*          /  302
/merch              /  302
/merch/*            /  302
/admin              /  302
/admin/*            /  302
/api/*              /  302
/tickets            /  302
/tickets/*          /  302
/vvip               /  302
/vvip/*             /  302
